4. Remove the index on 'cuisine' and observe how the query performance changes for cuisine-based searches. Briefly describe your findings in 2-3 sentences.

->  db.restaurants.dropIndex("cuisine_1")
->  Findings : After removing the cuisine index, MongoDB will generally use a COLLSCAN for the cuisine-only search because the remaining compound index starts with location, not cuisine. On a small collection of 10 documents the actual execution time may change very little, but on a large collection the indexed search would normally examine fewer documents and be faster.


